---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How many cold emails can I send per day?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "From a warmed-up domain: 20-50 per mailbox, scaling to 200-500 across multiple mailboxes. Exceeding this on a new domain is the fastest route to spam folders."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Does using multiple domains help?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Yes: spreading across 2-5 domains with separate inboxes isolates reputation damage. Each domain needs its own authentication and warm-up."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What bounce rate is acceptable for cold email?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Under 2% for verified lists; under 5% for semi-verified. Above that, your list quality (or verification tool) is the problem."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Should I use a subdomain for cold email?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Yes: mail.yourdomain.com isolates campaign reputation from your main domain. It needs its own SPF, DKIM, and DMARC records."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How do I avoid spam traps?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Never use purchased or scraped lists. Verify addresses before sending. Remove unengaged contacts after 90 days."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Can I use the same domain for cold and transactional?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Strongly discouraged: one bad campaign can affect password resets and receipts. Use separate subdomains at minimum."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Cold Email Deliverability: Staying Out of Spam | PromptDNS"
  description="Cold email deliverability: authentication, warm-up, volume control, and list quality for outbound campaigns that land in the inbox."
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Cold Email Deliverability</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">Cold Email Deliverability</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Cold email faces the hardest deliverability test: unsolicited mail to people who haven't opted in. Authentication, warm-up, and list quality aren't optional; they're the minimum to avoid the spam folder.</p>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">The compliance foundation</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li class="leading-relaxed">SPF, DKIM, and DMARC configured and passing: the <a href="/">homepage scanner</a> verifies all three in one pass.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">A custom domain (never a free address) with a verified sending subdomain.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Reverse DNS (PTR) on your sending IP, matching your HELO name.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">A working unsubscribe mechanism: one-click for Gmail/Yahoo compliance.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Volume discipline</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li class="leading-relaxed">Start a new domain at 10-20 emails per day, doubling weekly.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Never exceed 50% of your daily capacity in a single burst.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Separate cold outreach from transactional mail on different domains or subdomains.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Keep daily volume below 10% of your total sent history for the identity.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Content that avoids filters</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li class="leading-relaxed">No URL shorteners (they hide destination and trigger filters).</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Minimal HTML; plain text or light formatting performs better for cold.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">No spam-trigger words in subject lines (free, guaranteed, act now).</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Personalization that’s real (name, company, context), not mail-merge tokens.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">One clear call to action; no link farms.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Monitoring</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li class="leading-relaxed">Track bounce rate (under 2%), complaint rate (under 0.1%), and reply rate.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Check <a href="/blacklist-checker/">blocklists</a> weekly.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Use Google Postmaster Tools for domain reputation trends.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Run the <a href="/">homepage scanner</a> after any infrastructure change.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How many cold emails can I send per day?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">From a warmed-up domain: 20-50 per mailbox, scaling to 200-500 across multiple mailboxes. Exceeding this on a new domain is the fastest route to spam folders.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does using multiple domains help?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes: spreading across 2-5 domains with separate inboxes isolates reputation damage. Each domain needs its own authentication and warm-up.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What bounce rate is acceptable for cold email?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Under 2% for verified lists; under 5% for semi-verified. Above that, your list quality (or verification tool) is the problem.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Should I use a subdomain for cold email?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes: mail.yourdomain.com isolates campaign reputation from your main domain. It needs its own SPF, DKIM, and DMARC records.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I avoid spam traps?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Never use purchased or scraped lists. Verify addresses before sending. Remove unengaged contacts after 90 days.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I use the same domain for cold and transactional?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Strongly discouraged: one bad campaign can affect password resets and receipts. Use separate subdomains at minimum.</p></details></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Related</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2"><li><a href="/why-emails-go-to-spam/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Why emails go to spam →</a></li><li><a href="/email-sending-reputation/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Email sender reputation →</a></li><li><a href="/email-deliverability/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Email deliverability hub →</a></li></ul>

    <div class="mt-10 flex items-center gap-3 rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/40 px-5 py-3">
      <span class="grid h-9 w-9 place-items-center rounded-full bg-gradient-to-br from-accent to-violet font-display text-xs font-bold text-canvas">PD</span>
      <div>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">PromptDNS Team</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint">Last updated: August 2026</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
